=== Baseline NFR harness complete source ===
     1	#!/usr/bin/env python3
     2	"""AI.10 NFR harness runner (T-NFR-001 … T-NFR-004) — CP-8 scope.
     3
     4	Honesty rules (AI.13 / ADR-P2-010) applied here:
     5
     6	* **T-NFR-004** (queue bounds & priorities) is an in-process law and is
     7	  therefore measured and asserted exactly as AI.10 specifies.
     8	* **T-NFR-001** (analysis p95 < 400 ms) and **T-NFR-002** (submission ACK
     9	  p95 < 200 ms) are measured *in this environment* against in-repo fixtures
    10	  and the fake responder (no network) and are labelled ``SANDBOX-PARTIAL``:
    11	  AI.10 rule 5 requires the run on the actual target device with 30 % headroom
    12	  before live deployment — that measurement is an OWNER procedure and is never
    13	  claimed here.
    14	* **T-NFR-003** (CPU < 20 %, memory < 400 MB over 60 min) is sampled for
    15	  ``--minutes`` (default 1) and always labelled OWNER-VERIFY, because the
    16	  60-minute on-device run is the acceptance condition.
    17
    18	Usage
    19	-----
    20	    python3 scripts/run_nfr_harness.py [--json] [--minutes 1] [--decisions 200]
    21
    22	Exit codes: 0 measured within AI.7 bounds (sandbox labels attached) · 1 a
    23	bound was exceeded · 2 harness error.
    24	"""
    25
    26	from __future__ import annotations
    27
    28	import argparse
    29	import asyncio
    30	import json
    31	import math
    32	import os
    33	import sys
    34	import time
    35	from pathlib import Path
    36	from statistics import quantiles
    37	from typing import Any, Dict, List
    38
    39	REPO_ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parents[1]
